{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs/protocol.md at exact 53537a58559861905b1b050487fcfd5f7f22341b on request/amend4-contract, under promise git:sha1…6c8e89c on request git:sha1…24b01c9\n\nContract amendment 4 revision 2: answers review 2e38de90. One chunking rule (R-LOG-18): in the new layout any log file over B=8 MiB, including an old unpublished entry, is a directory of 8 MiB chunks at the same path; an oversized entry's segment line is a ChunkedLine stub (length, SHA-256), and verify reassembles and checks the original hash and signature. R-LOG-20 keeps every pushed commit outstanding, recorded before its first push, resolved only by ref read-back; refusals, read-back at the parent, expiry and revocation resolve nothing; a late own commit is confirmed, not treated as another writer. The 1 MiB entry, policy and checker-config bounds and the 256-checker cap are removed; every system event is recorded in full; one deterministic fan-out rule (R-LOG-19) keeps every tree under about 397 KB. New acceptance cases for the counterexample, delayed earlier push, and large notify, revert, activation, retained-prefix and 5 million entries. Root gates exit 0.","body":{"commit":"53537a58559861905b1b050487fcfd5f7f22341b","path":"docs/protocol.md"}}